---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
---

<ContentPage
	title="Features | PAN Card Photo & Signature Resizer"
	description="Explore the PAN card photo resizer features: photo and signature crop modes, adjustable dimensions, JPEG export under 50 KB, and private in-browser processing."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/features/"
	eyebrow="Tool features"
	heading="Useful features for PAN card photo and signature resizing"
	intro="Prepare both image types with a focused online PAN card tool. Adjust the crop and dimensions, review a JPEG preview, and keep image processing on your device."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Photo and signature modes</h2>
		<p>
			Switch between Photograph and Signature modes to start from
			different editable dimensions. The photo preset is 2.5 × 3.5 cm and
			the signature preset is 4.5 × 2 cm. These are starting points, not
			universal application rules; change them to the specifications
			shown by the service where you are applying.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Flexible crop and output</h2>
		<p>
			Move the crop frame to position your image and adjust its corners
			while preserving its proportions. Set the width and height in
			centimetres, choose 200, 300, or 600 DPI, and preview the pixel
			dimensions. Export a JPEG with a 50 KB target. When a complex image
			cannot meet that limit at the minimum quality, the tool reports the
			issue instead of saving an oversized file.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Local, private editing</h2>
		<p>
			Image selection, cropping, preview, and export run in your browser.
			Your image is not uploaded to this website, and the original source
			is not overwritten. Use a clear source image for the best result;
			resizing cannot restore detail lost to blur or poor lighting.
		</p>
	</section>
	<p>
		For an NSDL PAN card photo resizer or UTI PAN card photo resizer
		workflow, check the current portal requirements before using your
		downloaded file.
		<a class="text-link" href="/#requirements">Review the image requirements</a>.
	</p>
</ContentPage>
